<title>USA: Navistar picks Mexican site for new plant.</title>
<headline>Navistar picks Mexican site for new plant.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Navistar International Corp said Tuesday it had selected a 270-acre site in Escobedo, near Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico, for its new truck manufacturing plant.</p>
<p>Last month the company's board authorized a $167 million capital expenditure for plant construction.</p>
<p>Work is to begin by year-end. The facility is designed to assemble medium- and heavy-duty trucks on two lines at a planned daily production rate of 65 trucks on one shift. Production is scheduled to start in 1998.</p>
<p>Navistar manufactures buses, trucks and diesel engines.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
